public.prompt:
Read this supplied identity policy and decide each request outcome. Scope: only these identity statements, with no other policies. Compare action, resource and both supplied principal-tag conditions; distinguish implicit from explicit denial.
Here, the resource ending in `sandbox-orders/*` matches objects under `sandbox-orders/`. `StringEquals` requires the named principal-tag value to equal `yes`.
```json
{
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::sandbox-orders/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/approved": "yes"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::sandbox-orders/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/blocked": "yes"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

